#X text 215 80 Allpass filter is a signal processing filter that passes
all frequencies equally in gain \, but changes the phase relationship
among various frequencies.;
#X text 215 135 Most types of filter reduce the amplitude (i.e. the
magnitude) of the signal applied to it for some values of frequency
\, whereas the all-pass filter allows all frequencies through without
changes in level.;
#X text 215 205 Calculates coefficients for transfer function: H(z)=(b0
